The assembler algorithms were translated from TPDE's C++ assembler and
modified, and then rewritten in library passes. Byte storage and encodings
are generated from a buffer schema. Stable chunk storage and mutex lifecycle
are lowered by src/declarative/lang/stable_index.coil and mutex.coil, retaining
the same attribution as the assembler. CIR and aggregate-copy analysis originated
in coil-tpde and are now library passes too. Their types and operations are
numbered in src/declarative/cir/cir.ops, where each operation is said once.
See src/compiler/declarative/NOTICE for the rest of the backend.

